    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Black & White 050505 is the fourteenth studio album of original material by Simple Minds, released in September 2005 on Sanctuary Records. The title refers to the date the recording was completed, 05/05/05, and the album was praised as a return to the band’s expansive, polished rock sound, with “Home” serving as the best-known single.\n\nRecorded in the Netherlands and mixed by Bob Clearmountain, the album blends atmospheric keyboards, driving guitars, and Jim Kerr’s assured vocals into a concise nine-track set. Its sound recalls the sweep of earlier Simple Minds albums such as Sparkle in the Rain and Once Upon a Time, while still feeling modern and focused, and it was generally received as a strong comeback after a quieter period for the band.\n\nThe original release ran just over 41 minutes, though later editions added bonus tracks such as “Too Much Television,” “Bird On a Wire,” and “Mighty Joe Moon.” The album also achieved modest commercial success, including a Gold certification in Italy, underscoring its status as one of Simple Minds’ more notable 2000s releases.",
